# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is gitignored.
#
# NOTE: put your real key in .env.local, NOT in this file. This template is
# committed to git, so a key here would be published (and harvested — bots scan
# public repos for exactly this).
#
# YouTube Data API v3 key — the app's entire content source.
#
# Get one:
#   1. https://console.cloud.google.com  ->  create (or pick) a project
#   2. APIs & Services -> Library -> enable "YouTube Data API v3"
#   3. APIs & Services -> Credentials -> Create credentials -> API key
#   4. Under "API restrictions", restrict it to YouTube Data API v3.
#
# Do NOT add an HTTP referrer restriction. This key is used from the SERVER
# (server/youtubeSearch.js), and server-to-server requests send no Referer
# header, so a referrer restriction would reject every request. Referrer locking
# only applies to keys called from a browser — which this one deliberately isn't.
#
# The name has no VITE_ prefix on purpose: Vite inlines VITE_-prefixed variables
# into the client bundle, which would publish the key to every visitor. Keeping
# it unprefixed means only the server can read it.
#
# In production this same variable is set in the Render dashboard, not here.
#
# Quota: 10,000 units/day, ~101 units per uncached search (~100 searches/day).
# The server caches results for 12h and shares that cache across all visitors.
YOUTUBE_API_KEY=
